From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:33:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: ease the tab sheet close cover and bottom button row
 into the real bar

While the bottom tab sheet closes, the five-button row and the gray band
under it changed in a single frame at the hand-off. Before it, the cover
that holds the bar's place was painted in the sheet's chrome colour, cast a
20dp elevation shadow that read as a gray band across the seam and the
plus button, and started below the top of the bottom toolbar, so a strip of
it stayed uncovered. The bottom-bar travel that hides the compositor's
button row snapped from its last spring value to 0 on the same frame as the
scene layer and the faded icons were restored, so the plus button's
highlight popped to its resting look.

On the close path only (the way down, the park and the reveal), the cover
now has no shadow, reaches up over the whole bottom toolbar and eases its
fill from the sheet chrome colour to the real bar surface over the existing
hand-off fade. The bottom-bar travel is held at the value it had when the
close began and eased to 0 over the same fade, driving the row's alpha,
visibility and the compositor layer from that one value. The open path, the
settled bar and everything after the close chrome is finished are unchanged,
and so are the url bitmap, the icon copies, the text shift and the page and
top toolbar restore.

The unit tests cover the cover having no shadow and spanning the toolbar, the
cover colour and the row's travel and alpha being continuous across the
hand-off frame and easing monotonically to the resting state, and the open
path leaving all of it alone.
